hey everyone persia here and we got our  hands on the halo infinite technical  preview and while it is definitely an  early build we still thought it would be  great to put together some important  things that you should know about  infinite go ahead and leave a like and  subscribe and let's hop right into it  the mini map in halo infinite works a  little bit differently than many maps of  halo's past in terms of how you are  detected by the map while the map is  always visible that doesn't necessarily  mean your enemies are going to show up  on the map just because they're in range  of course in the past crouching was a  good way to avoid detection but now you  can crouch and walk without being  detected this leaves sprinting shooting  your gun or taking damage as the  requirements needed to pop up on the  mini map so if you are used to using the  map for intel you might get snuck up on  one or two more times than expected  until you get used to this change halo  infinite also has a ping system and you  can also get points and assists for  pinging enemies correctly and helping  out the team along with that the ai  callouts are surprisingly good so if  you're not on comms then there are  definitely more options in infinite to  get some sort of communication with your  teammates without physically being on  the mic  this could just be my experience but it  felt like armor and health were slightly  redistributed usually in the past when  you broke someone's armor you knew that  they were one shot and they were close  to dead but in infinite it felt like you  had a little bit more health to give  meaning you could get yourself out of  tricky situations or have a better  chance at surviving with that in mind  making sure that the marksman weapons  were on our team were definitely a  priority as they seem to be the best  weapon at finishing cracked targets  maybe not including grenades but we'll  get to that later lens flare is in halo  infinite however i did not notice this  until the final day of the preview where  we actually got to play against real  people i guess the bots didn't have much  of a use of adsing or weren't using guns  that required them to ads so i didn't  really notice it throughout the first  few days of the preview but playing  against actual people you can definitely  tell and it even helped me spot enemies  or win vr battles so let me know down  below what you think of lens flare being  in the game  the abilities in halo infinite are  actually super interesting but first  things first if you want to pick one up  all you got to do is run or walk over it  if you have empty pockets it'll be  picked up automatically if you don't  have empty pockets then you're gonna  need to pick it up manually by holding x  the deployable shield is a lot less  annoying than i thought it was gonna be  it definitely has a long start-up time  as well so you're not going to want to  toss it in the middle of a gun fight  because you're probably going to die  before it even activates however if you  can place it down at a popular choke  point ahead of time you're always going  to have the advantage in a one-on-one  the shield itself does take damage and  chunks of it will disappear once it  takes too much damage but it's still a  great option if you're trying to get a  leg up on the competition or if you're  trying to pass a very heated choke point  with a little bit more safety the  grapple is probably my favorite ability  of all of the abilities so far it adds  some much needed variety to the vertical  movement of the game but it's not a part  of our main kit like i thought it was  going to be it's an ability that spawns  on the ground that you will have to pick  up and comes with a limited number of  uses so you also have to be strategic  with how you use it activecamo and  overshield are making their return to  halo infinite but they work a little bit  differently than how they used to they  are abilities after all which means you  will have to pick them up from their  spawn point and then you'll have to  manually apply it to get its special  effect this means you have to be smart  about picking it up and you have to be  safe about when you actually activate it  because you can die before it is fully  active and it will drop on the floor  which means your opponent can pick it up  instead  [Music]  we got to check out three of the maps  during the preview which were live fire  recharge and bizarre they were all  pretty small but exactly what you would  expect for a 4v4 slayer arena style map  which made grenades even more dangerous  and teamwork even more important but i'm  definitely here for it one of my  favorite things though about each map  was that power weapons and marksman  weapons would rotate with each and every  match so you weren't guaranteed to have  a br or commando or rockets or a sniper  but it definitely added some variety and  kind of changed how my team would  approach certain matches if a more  favorable power weapon was spawning that  match well we would favor that but if  the marksman weapons were a little bit  more in our favor then we might go that  way instead i think this is awesome and  i hope it's something that we see  consistently moving forward  now it's time to talk a little bit about  general speed and general movement per  spartan i'm not going to talk about the  grapple hook because it's not a part of  our main kit and we already talked about  how awesome it was earlier but there are  some other big things to note about the  new movement in halo infinite of course  we have our crouch and walk speed that  feels very traditional very halo like in  terms of not being very fast but we also  have the return of the sprint and we can  also slide this means that the thrust  the shoulder charge and the ground pound  for halo 5 are definitely out the window  but the sprint got a couple of buffs  which is leading me to believe that this  is going to be the main movement tool so  with sprinting in halo infinite you can  reload and you can regain your shields  while sprinting those of you familiar  with halo 5 knew that you couldn't quite  take off running until your shields were  already starting to recharge or else you  were going to be one shot forever but  now that is not the case which means if  you see some grenades coming your way  you better start running because you  might get caught in a really sticky  situation and honestly the grenades  single-handedly made me miss having a  thrust because that was my go-to tactic  in halo 5 when i saw nades coming my way  i would just thrust out of there but now  that's not so much the case which means  you have to prioritize your spread and  get a good judgment of your surroundings  much earlier than you used to  time to go ahead and talk about some of  the weapons starting with the pistol it  was definitely a polarizing feeling  using the pistol because some moments  when all of my headshots are perfect and  my aim is on point i felt i was as close  to a halo 1 pistol as i could get but if  those headshots were not accurate and i  was getting one too many body shots or  shoulder shots we easily crept into halo  2 pistol territory which is not what we  want especially when there is no dual  wield but if you got the aim to back it  up the pistol is definitely a deadly one  in  infinite perfect the br the good old  battle rifle is definitely making a  strong return to forum in infinite the  br has probably been one of my absolute  favorite weapons in the entire series  since its existence but it's super  satisfying to use an infinite which  definitely makes me one happy spartan  you can still get those perfect four  shot kills that are always glorious to  get and you also become infinitely more  dangerous at the high ground cleaning up  all those cracked targets for your team  i would highly recommend prioritizing  marksman weapons but the br above them  all if you want to be the one to clean  up those skills and bring home the dub  for your team i knew the skewer was  dangerous but i didn't truly understand  how dangerous until we got to play a few  pvp matches towards the end of the  preview any player with great aim is  gonna get easy killing sprees with the  skewers so everyone's gonna want to  watch out for this weapon because i  believe it is a one-touch kill no matter  where it hits you so a strong power  weapon for sure and if you got the aim  for it definitely make good use of it  the commando is a new marksman weapon in  halo infinite and while it is an  automatic gun i think it's much stronger  when you burst fire it because the  recoil is extremely wild it's very  unwieldy and a spray and pray method  with this gun doesn't really give you  accurate results especially considering  that there is a bit of bloom that you  have to manage now if you get used to  burst firing it it could be just as  strong as a br especially from long  distances but you definitely need a bit  more control with this weapon when the  game gives you an advice tip that tells  you you should start or end your gun  battle with a grenade i think it's safe  to say that grenades are pretty strong  and i do feel like throughout most of  the preview i probably dyed two grenades  more than i died to guns but that could  also be an ai thing because they seem to  throw the perfect grenade every single  time the perfect bounce the perfect  trajectory the perfect timing you name  it that is how these bots were throwing  the grenades when we did play some pvp  matches at the end of the preview the  grenades were a lot less accurate and i  did find myself dying to them a lot less  but they're still very powerful and the  blast radius is so strong so be careful  for those needs and keep in mind that  you also have grenades so use them  wisely especially if you see a lot of  people in an area because that's easy  doubles triples and overkills the  gravity hammer is making its return in  halo infinite and it's as deadly as ever  i initially didn't think it was that  strong because when i used it against  higher level bots they flat out  destroyed me before i ever got close  enough to actually get a swing in there  but when i played against actual players  and had some backup from my team or vice  versa fighting against someone else who  had backup from their team the hammer  became way more difficult to deal with  so that's worth keeping in mind as well  that some of these weapons are stronger  as long as you're using some teamwork  while there are many more weapons in  halo infinite the last one i'm gonna  talk about in this video is going to be  the pulse carbine the pulse carbine is a  really interesting weapon and it shoots  a three round burst of plasma bullets  these bullets kind of inherited some  halo 2 plasma pistol traits in terms  that there is a little bit of tracking  on the bullet and it only takes one  burst to break your shield it only takes  two bursts to kill you completely so  it's definitely a dangerous weapon in  the right hands but honestly i think  it's the most dangerous if you're  rolling around with a teammate who's  using a marksman weapon because then in  theory you and your teammate can go  around two-shotting every person you  come across but it also means you can  keep a marksman weapon on your secondary  and do the two shotting yourself if your  aim with the pulse carbine is on point  [Music]  alright everyone that is a wrap on this  video but that's not a wrap on halo  infinite previews because the devs have  already confirmed that more previews and  more flights are on the way for halo  infinite before launch this means you  can head over to halowaypoint.com  and you still have time to sign up for  one of those future previews by  following all the instructions for the  halo insider program don't miss out  because this game is great and you're  going to want to give it a try for  yourself and i guarantee y